    <string name="guide_title_liquid">Water Level Sensor: Calibration Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_title_temp">Temperature Sensor: Calibration Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_title_tds">Dissolved Solids Sensor: Calibration Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_title_ph">pH Level Sensor: Calibration Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_liquid">1. Empty or lower the tank water below the sensor trigger point.\n2. Confirm the app shows a low / empty reading.\n3. Raise the water to the normal fill line.\n4. Confirm the app shows a full / normal reading.\n5. Adjust the sensor position if the trigger point is off.</string>
    <string name="guide_temp">1. Place the sensor in a verified ice-water bath (0 °C / 32 °F).\n2. Wait 60 seconds for the reading to stabilise.\n3. Optionally repeat with a warm reference (e.g. 40 °C / 104 °F).\n4. Note any offset and adjust in your controller if needed.</string>
    <string name="guide_tds">1. Rinse the probe with distilled water.\n2. Submerge in a 0 ppm (DI) solution and wait 30 seconds for a near-zero reading.\n3. Rinse, then submerge in a known TDS calibration solution (e.g. 342 ppm or 1000 ppm).\n4. Wait for the reading to match the solution value, then rinse before returning to the tank.</string>
    <string name="guide_ph">1. Rinse the probe with distilled water.\n2. Submerge in pH 7 buffer solution for 60 seconds.\n3. Rinse again, then submerge in pH 4 (or pH 10) buffer for 60 seconds.\n4. Rinse thoroughly. The probe is ready.</string>
